WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.169
The 2024 Republican race is

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:04.170
getting more crowded.

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.238
South Carolina GOP

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:06.039
Senator Tim Scott

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:07.140
filed his paperwork

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.109
today, launching his fundraising effort.

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:09.843
He'll make the official

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:10.910
campaign announcement

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.512
at home in South Carolina on Monday.

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:13.680
And as noted,

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:14.881
we are told the Florida governor, Ron

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:16.383
DeSantis, will officially file

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:18.385
his paperwork mid-week next week.

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:20.253
Here you see the leading names already

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:21.488
in about to get in.

00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:23.423
And several others who promise decisions

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:25.025
relatively soon

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:25.492
or great

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:27.494
reporters are back at the table with me.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.161
Let's start

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:29.496
with Senator Scott

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:32.065
Everyone else you have Trump,

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:33.033
you have well behind him

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.467
in the national polls, DeSantis,

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:35.368
and then you have everybody else

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:36.636
way, way back.

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:37.137
And they're trying

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:38.838
to find their piece of it.

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:39.406
The New York Times

00:00:39.406 --> 00:00:40.206
saying this about Senator

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:41.041
Scott this morning.

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:42.809
There's little evidence so far that Mr.

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:44.411
Scott's message strikes a chord

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:46.579
with the populist base of the modern GOP,

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:47.881
which for the last several years

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:49.816
has been led by a former TV star

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:51.184
who likes to fight again.

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:52.185
Back to the same conversation

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:53.787
we're having about getting at DeSantis

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:54.521
and Pence, his idea

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:55.422
about limited concern.

00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:56.256
That's the challenge

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:57.123
for these candidates.

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:58.291
Which Republican Party

00:00:58.291 --> 00:00:59.292
are you competing in?

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:00.493
Are you appealing to? Right.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:02.529
And can you effectively try to

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:03.596
actually galvanize

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:04.464
some of the Trump base

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:06.199
while going with a different message?

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:07.300
And to be clear,

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:07.867
Tim Scott's

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.469
message is quite different here.

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:10.904
I would say even more than are now.

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:11.471
Even more.

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:13.506
But also, it's different than DeSantis

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:14.140
as well.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.075
Well,

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:16.709
you know, as my colleagues wrote,

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:18.211
while Trump is talking about,

00:01:19.446 --> 00:01:20.580
you know, needing to reform

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.281
law enforcement

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:21.781
agencies, he's

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.316
attacking law enforcement agencies

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:25.819
at a time with his rhetoric and

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:27.854
sowing sort of distrust as well.

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:30.790
Tim Scott's message is much more kind of

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:31.958
sunny language.

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:34.527
Ronald Reagan, this going away.

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:37.497
So is that also going to appeal to a base

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:39.199
that has actually been engaged

00:01:39.199 --> 00:01:40.433
by Trump's language,

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:41.701
which I don't think anyone would describe

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:42.469
as Sunny?

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:44.003
He launched a $6 million

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:45.672
ad buy in Iowa, New Hampshire today,

00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:46.639
which is $6 million.

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:47.607
That's a lot of money.

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:48.374
If people have stayed home.

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:49.342
However,

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:51.010
Trump has 100 plus million dollars.

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:52.479
DeSantis has 100 plus million dollars.

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:53.279
As the challenge

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:54.848
is to prove to prove what?

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:55.348
To prove

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:56.316
that you can start

00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:57.884
at least inching up to keep the money

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:59.085
coming for sure.

00:01:59.085 --> 00:02:00.820
And I think also introducing himself,

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:01.287
that's one thing

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:02.021
that Senator Scott

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:04.357
absolutely needs to do.

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:05.725
He has a lot of goodwill.

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:06.860
I was out with him in Iowa

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:07.760
a couple of weeks ago

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:08.261
when he was doing

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:09.395
an exploratory committee.

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:11.531
He's one is getting about four bites

00:02:11.531 --> 00:02:12.332
out of the apple here

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:12.966
as he announced he's

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:13.833
running for president.

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:14.901
And Republicans

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:15.935
there were very eager

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:17.270
to hear his message.

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.239
So intrigued by his biography.

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:20.707
My question for Senator Scott,

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:22.208
though, is a biography

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:23.443
enough of a message

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:24.878
or does he need something

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:25.979
a little bit more than that?

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:27.280
And he does have a hopeful,

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:28.848
optimistic view.

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:31.484
I don't see a lot of demand

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:32.986
for that necessarily.

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:34.287
But without a doubt,

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:35.455
he is going to do this.

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:36.990
And I think he is going to have a

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.558
you know, he's the only senator running.

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:39.659
So he'll have

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:41.761
some other support from senators as well.

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:43.163
So, you know, Monday it started.

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:44.164
I think that's a key point.

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:45.365
Trump is a grievance party.

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:46.900
Can you pull it back to a either

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.201
a policy, an ideological

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:49.235
or an optimistic party

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:50.103
that that's one of the challenges.

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:51.538
Just look at the polling right now.

00:02:51.538 --> 00:02:52.005
It's Trump

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:52.539
at 43,

00:02:52.539 --> 00:02:54.240
DeSantis at 20, then Pence, Haley,

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.042
Christie and Tim Scott.

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:56.943
These are national polls.

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:58.044
You can change these numbers

00:02:58.044 --> 00:02:59.112
by winning Iowa

00:02:59.112 --> 00:03:00.547
or surprising in Iowa or New Hampshire

00:03:00.547 --> 00:03:01.581
or South Carolina.

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:03.316
Scott from South Carolina, Nikki Haley,

00:03:03.316 --> 00:03:04.417
also from South Carolina,

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:05.718
the former governor, the former U.N.

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:06.452
ambassador.

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:07.887
So let's listen to a little bit here.

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:08.788
She got into the race.

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:10.223
She says, I'm the alternative to Trump.

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:11.224
You don't want to go back.

00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:12.525
She's trying to figure out her place,

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:13.526
especially with DeSantis

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:14.627
getting so much attention.

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:15.828
This is about January six.

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:17.430
Donald Trump calls it a beautiful day.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:18.898
Nikki Haley says no

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:22.802
What I will say about January 6th,

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.338
I will continue to say

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:26.406
it was a terrible day.

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:27.540
It was not a beautiful day.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.242
It was a terrible day.

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:31.444
And we don't ever want that to happen.

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:34.981
You break the law, you pay the price.

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.015
And on the question,

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:37.116
she has come under some heat

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:38.818
on the question of abortion rights.

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:39.886
She says she's pro-life.

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:41.221
She says as a state governor,

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:42.989
she would sign restrictions on abortion.

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:44.791
She says it's dishonest to talk now

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:45.825
about whether it's a 12 week

00:03:45.825 --> 00:03:47.760
or 15 week or 20 week federal ban

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.128
because she says the votes in the Senate

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:50.096
simply aren't there.

00:03:50.096 --> 00:03:52.265
And she says she's glad the Supreme Court

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:53.132
overturned Roe,

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:54.133
sent this back to the state.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.868
Now, she says get the judges out of it.

00:03:58.037 --> 00:03:59.038
You never should have

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:01.241
had unelected justices

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:03.443
deciding something, that person,

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:06.879
because the idea of life and abortion

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:09.515
is personal for everyone, not just women.

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:12.585
Now, the unelected justices

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:14.687
have gone back and ruled and I think.

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:14.921
Right.

00:04:14.921 --> 00:04:17.223
It is wrong and put it back in the states

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:19.025
close to the people

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:20.927
where the people can decide

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:22.428
what they want.

00:04:23.196 --> 00:04:24.731
She says she hopes states

00:04:24.731 --> 00:04:25.665
pass restrictions,

00:04:25.665 --> 00:04:26.532
but if they don't, that's up

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:27.267
to the people there

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:28.801
and she can accept that.

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:29.969
The question is, what lane is that?

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:30.436
Is there

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:31.838
is there such a lane in the republic

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:33.606
where she's trying to sound like is it?

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:34.340
I don't know what to call it.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:35.074
Is it more centrist?

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:35.908
Is it more reasonable?

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:36.843
Is it more open minded?

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:37.410
I don't know what it is,

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:38.645
but does it exist? Right.

00:04:38.645 --> 00:04:39.379
To go back

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:40.079
to what

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:42.181
we've all kind of been saying here is

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:43.916
how is the party going to define itself?

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:45.318
And that really has been the question

00:04:45.318 --> 00:04:46.486
since Trump.

00:04:46.486 --> 00:04:47.887
Right because even,

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:48.221
you know,

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:49.522
when I talked to people on Capitol

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:50.690
Hill, privately, Republicans

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:51.924
are obsessed with Tim Scott.

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:54.093
They really think he could bring

00:04:54.093 --> 00:04:55.395
the Republican Party

00:04:55.395 --> 00:04:56.162
back to what

00:04:56.162 --> 00:04:57.630
it was on principle,

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.265
but also be able to have

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:01.100
these bigger conversations

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.802
on different, different subject matters.

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:04.537
But I think that someone like Scott,

00:05:04.537 --> 00:05:05.672
someone like Haley,

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:07.040
I don't know what that path is

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:07.940
because it's not middle ground.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:08.741
They won't say they're moderate.

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:09.942
They won't say they're pragmatic.

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:12.178
They're tried to really find a lane here

00:05:12.378 --> 00:05:13.746
at a time when the party doesn't

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:15.715
even want to really talk about abortion.

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:16.516
They don't want to talk

00:05:16.516 --> 00:05:18.918
about those different, you know,

00:05:18.918 --> 00:05:20.420
when should abortion

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:22.121
be, when should abortion bans

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:24.023
be happening, those kinds of things.

00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:24.991
They don't want to have that debate

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:26.025
right now.

00:05:26.159 --> 00:05:26.959
When do they have it?

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:27.927
I'm not entirely sure.

00:05:27.927 --> 00:05:29.896
And most of the primaries are closed,

00:05:29.896 --> 00:05:31.164
meaning only Republican voters,

00:05:31.164 --> 00:05:32.398
not all, but most of them are closed,

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:33.900
meaning only Republican voters.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:34.934
And the Republican Party

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:36.903
has become more Trumpy, unless,

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:38.104
I would say, you know,

00:05:38.104 --> 00:05:39.105
more of a grievance party

00:05:39.105 --> 00:05:40.006
than a smile party,

00:05:40.006 --> 00:05:41.074
like a Tim Scott, if you will, I.

